            <ArticleTitle>Preventable effects of bare-metal stent on restenosis after everolimus-eluting stent deployment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>434-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00380-014-0588-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes a patient who underwent implantation of a bare-metal stent (BMS) for the treatment of everolimus-eluting stent (EES) restenosis caused by chronic stent recoil, and the BMS successfully escaped from duplicate restenosis and target lesion revascularization (TLR).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
